List a table's new columns as soon as the commit that changed them lands.

A table's entry in its schema's table set is the table as a bind last loaded
it. Binds load the table again every time; listings (duckdb_columns(), and
the information_schema and pg_catalog views over it) show the entry as it is.
After a commit that changed a table's columns or properties, the entry still
held the table from before the commit, so an ALTER TABLE's columns showed in
listings only once a later statement happened to bind the table: ten ADD
COLUMNs in a row listed the first nine, and SQLAlchemy's reflection, which
reads the listings right after its DDL, saw the old shape. Once such a commit
lands, the entry is replaced by one not loaded yet, which the next bind loads;
Igloo loads unloaded tables before every statement that lists columns.

